+  <p class="story">In the meeting <code>/sc:workflow</code> was described as "task builder light": faster and cheaper. It assumes you have done your homework, or lets you tell it plainly in a prompt what to plan. The rule of thumb given there: a plan made by an <code>sc:</code> command is followed up by an <code>sc:</code> command, and a plan from a plain slash command, for the most part, by a plain one. The guide's rule wins: when an approved plan already exists, use its own executor and do not rebuild it. A <code>/sc:workflow</code> package runs with <code>/sc:implement</code>; an existing MDTM task file runs with <code>/task</code>.</p>
